From: Nfrastack <code@nfrastack.com>
Date: Thu, 23 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix: timeline messages not rendering after sync optimization

Bug: Commit 15699c557d removed this.setState({ clientSyncState }) from
the onSync handler to reduce re-renders on every sync pulse. However,
onRoomTimeline can silently drop live events when:
  - messagePanel.current is null (panel not mounted yet)
  - stuckAtBottom is false (user scrolled up)

Without the periodic setState from onSync, missed events are never
recovered. They exist in the Matrix SDK's room timeline but never get
paginated into the TimelineWindow buffer and so never appear in React
state.

Furthermore, ClientEvent.Sync only fires on sync state transitions,
NOT on every sync response. So onSync cannot be relied upon to
periodically refresh the event list — the fix must happen entirely
within onRoomTimeline.

Fix:
1. Always paginate live events into the TimelineWindow buffer in
onRoomTimeline, even when the panel is not mounted or the user has
scrolled up. This ensures events are never dropped from the buffer.

2. Call reloadEvents() immediately after each paginate() call in the
early-return branches, so React state is updated with the buffered
event right away. This replaces the broken strategy of relying on
onSync to eventually pick up buffered events.

3. Keep the visibilitychange handler (also calling reloadEvents()) as
a safety net for paints the browser deferred while backgrounded.

4. Keep the onSync reloadEvents() call since it does help on sync
state transitions (initial load, reconnect, catchup).
diff --git a/apps/web/src/components/structures/TimelinePanel.tsx b/apps/web/src/components/structures/TimelinePanel.tsx
index 51bce161c7..2b29ea6904 100644
--- a/apps/web/src/components/structures/TimelinePanel.tsx
+++ b/apps/web/src/components/structures/TimelinePanel.tsx
@@ -306,6 +306,7 @@
         cli.on(RoomEvent.LocalEchoUpdated, this.onLocalEchoUpdated);
         cli.on(RoomEvent.AccountData, this.onAccountData);
         cli.on(MatrixEventEvent.Decrypted, this.onEventDecrypted);
+        document.addEventListener("visibilitychange", this.onPageVisibilityChange);
         cli.on(MatrixEventEvent.Replaced, this.onEventReplaced);
         cli.on(ClientEvent.Sync, this.onSync);
 
@@ -366,6 +367,7 @@
             this.readMarkerActivityTimer = null;
         }
 
+        document.removeEventListener("visibilitychange", this.onPageVisibilityChange);
         dis.unregister(this.dispatcherRef);
 
         const client = MatrixClientPeg.get();
@@ -683,13 +685,19 @@
         // updates from pagination will happen when the paginate completes.
         if (toStartOfTimeline || !data || !data.liveEvent) return;
 
-        if (!this.messagePanel.current?.getScrollState()) return;
+        if (!this.messagePanel.current?.getScrollState()) {
+            this.timelineWindow!.paginate(EventTimeline.FORWARDS, 1, false);
+            this.reloadEvents();
+            return;
+        }
 
         if (!this.messagePanel.current.getScrollState()?.stuckAtBottom) {
             // we won't load this event now, because we don't want to push any
             // events off the other end of the timeline. But we need to note
             // that we can now paginate.
             this.setState({ canForwardPaginate: true });
+            this.timelineWindow!.paginate(EventTimeline.FORWARDS, 1, false);
+            this.reloadEvents();
             return;
         }
 
@@ -901,10 +909,17 @@
     private onSync = (clientSyncState: SyncState, prevState: SyncState | null, data?: object): void => {
         if (this.unmounted) return;
         const nextSyncImpliesForwardPaginating = TimelinePanel.isSyncForwardPaginating(clientSyncState);
-        if (nextSyncImpliesForwardPaginating === this.syncImpliesForwardPaginating) return;
+        if (nextSyncImpliesForwardPaginating !== this.syncImpliesForwardPaginating) {
+            this.syncImpliesForwardPaginating = nextSyncImpliesForwardPaginating;
+        }
+        this.reloadEvents();
+    };
 
-        this.syncImpliesForwardPaginating = nextSyncImpliesForwardPaginating;
-        this.forceUpdate();
+    private onPageVisibilityChange = (): void => {
+        if (this.unmounted) return;
+        if (document.visibilityState === "visible") {
+            this.reloadEvents();
+        }
     };
 
     private static isSyncForwardPaginating(syncState: SyncState | null): boolean {
